  "applies_to": "SenseAir tSENSE wall sensors (CO2, temperature, RH) using their RS-485 port in BACnet MS/TP mode.",
  "summary": "The tSENSE is a wall CO2 sensor with temperature and humidity that can speak BACnet MS/TP on its RS-485 port. It reports CO2, temperature, RH and its three analog output voltages as AIs, a relay state BI and an ABC on/off BV; the AVs hold the MAC address, baud rate, sensor offsets, relay setpoint and the scaling of the three analog outputs.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 669010,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object names are generic (\"AI-1\" etc.); the descriptions come from the object table.",
    "AV-4 is shown as Reserved in the overview and has no object page, so it is left out.",
    "The object pages mark Present_Value RW on the AIs and BI too, but writes are only accepted while Out_Of_Service is true (an override); they are listed as read-only here.",
    "Device instance = 669 x 1000 + MAC address (default 669010) until a new instance is written; device name defaults to \"tSENSE\" + MAC.",
    "Source copy is the DwyerOmega-hosted \"BACnet on tSENSE\" TDE 102 rev 3 bundled after the tSENSE user manual."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet on tSENSE",
    "doc_number": "TDE 102",
    "revision_date": "2015-12-08",
    "url": "https://assets.dwyeromega.com/manuals/tsenseusermanualbacnetinfo-0.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "host": "DwyerOmega"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set the RS-485 protocol to BACnet (or Auto), then read CO2, temperature and humidity from AI-1 to AI-3. Relay state is on BI-1; the relay setpoint and hysteresis and the analog output scaling live in the AVs and only need setting once.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "AI-1",
        "why": "CO2, ppm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 2",
        "name": "AI-2",
        "why": "Room temperature, °C"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "AI-3",
        "why": "Room relative humidity"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1",
        "name": "BI-1",
        "why": "Relay state (CO2 above relay setpoint)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "MS/TP master at 9600, 19200, 38400, 57600, 76800 or 115200 baud; default MAC 10, default 9600 baud.",
      "MAC and baud can also be written via AV-1 and AV-2.",
      "With the RS-485 protocol set to Auto, the sensor listens to the bus and picks BACnet or Modbus on its own.",
      "No segmentation; max master 127 (writable)."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Writing an AI or BI Present_Value needs Out_Of_Service set true, which overrides the real reading.",
      "Changing the MAC also changes the default device instance and name unless they were written explicitly."
    ]
  },
